/*
 * Designed for a 1920x1080 context viewed from the couch: large type, high
 * contrast, generous spacing, and an unmissable focus treatment. Palette is
 * a deep blue-slate night background with a warm "tuner amber" accent used
 * for focus and selection, plus a red reserved for what is on air.
 *
 *   background   #0b1020, lit from the top left
 *   panel        #ffffff08 .. #ffffff14, rounded
 *   text         #e8edf7    muted #8593ab    faint #5a6478
 *   accent       #f5b453, as a bar #f7c26c -> #e9a13c with dark text #241604
 *   live         #ff5c5c (on air, recording now)
 *
 * The look follows jtplay's: rounded rows, focus as a solid accent bar with
 * dark text (as in Kodi), soft shadows, glass over the picture. It needs the
 * GPU (gradients, blur and shadows are shaders), which the console has since
 * Mesa came over Vulkan; the software renderer it was once drawn with could
 * do flat colour only.
 *
 * The per-view rules live in assets/css/; this file holds the palette note
 * and the global body scaffold that all of them build on.
 */

body {
	width: 100%;
	height: 100%;
	font-size: 26px;
	color: #e8edf7;
	background-color: #0b1020;
	decorator: radial-gradient(circle farthest-corner at 12% 0%, #1c2742 0%, #0b1020 55%);
	transition: background-color 0.25s cubic-out;
}
